<title>JAPAN: Toray to boost China units' capacity.</title>
<headline>Toray to boost China units' capacity.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toray Industries Inc said on Thursday it will invest 1.9 billion yen to help boost capacity at two Chinese joint ventures that it operates with Sakai Ovex Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The partners aim to double monthly production capacity at the dyeing and weaving joint ventures at a total cost of 5.5 billion yen, Toray said in a statement.</p>
<p>Of that amount, Toray will contribute 1.9 billion yen. Sakai Ovex will invest one billion yen and the rest will be raised by the Chinese ventures themselves in China, a Toray spokesman said.</p>
<p>Toray is a textiles maker and Sakai Ovex is a synthetic fabrics company.</p>
</text>
